    "GHA_idea_language_barrier": "The Language Barrier",
    "GHA_idea_language_barrier_desc": "Ghana's roots extend into two different European cultures; the country formed from the British Gold Coast colony and French Togo. With no standard language, the Ghana administration is divided between two systems, making unified reform almost impossible. It takes time for such a bilingual country to undergo standardization, and while Ghana has taken its first steps towards unification, the African state has a long way to go before its government can effectively coordinate.",
    "GHA_idea_bloated_high_command": "Bloated High Command",
    "GHA_idea_bloated_high_command_desc": "Many conflicts have stood in the path to Ghana's unification, and each new battle comes with extensive promotion. Ghana's military is unusual in that it is incredibly top-heavy, with countless numbers of high-ranking officers. With many prized officers looking to assert dominance over other prized officers, the army is plagued by countless rivalries and factions. Unfortunately, this has created an ineffective, incoherent military force in Ghana."
